# Reject heuristic world corrections

Reject heuristic map offsets, interior movements, global height raises, UV
mirrors, and other corrections not present in source evidence.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Reject heuristic map offsets, interior movements, global height raises, UV
  mirrors, and other corrections not present in source evidence.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency was recorded in the legacy TODO.

## Evidence

The world exporter publishes every normal exterior and interior FBX at the
source-authored global origin. Narrative map-family labels carry no coordinate
offset, source overlap is allowed, and bounds validation rejects only malformed
or non-finite source geometry rather than applying extent or height policy.

The production root policy performs one `ReflectX` basis conversion for FBX to
Unreal while preserving authored UV coordinates. Exterior and interior meshes
are copied into the structural guide with positions, normals, UVs, triangle
order, materials, and textures unchanged. The guide manifest validator requires
all spatial-correction flags to remain false and its Unreal import transform to
stay at identity. Source-backed coordinate transplants require compatible
topology and preserve the canonical material/UV presentation.

Definition-only review meshes are the one intentional exception: they are moved
into a deterministic gallery under `review/`, which is explicitly excluded from
the normal world import set and cannot alter production package coordinates.

Fresh stable-Rust tests passed the no-offset narrative grouping and the
no-height-policy
bounds validation, single-reflection UV contract, exact exterior/interior guide
copy, authored nested scenegraph translation, structural-guide manifest policy,
and source-backed coordinate-transplant regressions.
